    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

This example uses a nested loop to generate all possible 4-digit combinations and checks each one against a hypothetical `checkPin` function. In a real-world scenario, you would use more secure methods to check the password or PIN.

Keep in mind that bruteforcing can be time-consuming and inefficient, especially for complex passwords or large data sets. In some cases, it may not be the best approach, and alternative methods such as hash-based attacks or dictionary attacks may be more effective.

Bruteforcing should be used responsibly and ethically, as it can be used maliciously to gain unauthorized access to systems or data. Always respect privacy and security policies when working with passwords or sensitive information.

